From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/grate: arm connector hotplug detection once the connectors exist

drm_kms_helper_poll_init() runs before host1x_device_init() creates the
connectors, so the enable_hpd pass of drm_kms_helper_poll_enable() finds
none. Hotplug bridges, here HDMI through display-connector, then never get
their HPD callback: the interrupt fires (hpd_cb is NULL in
display_connector_hpd_irq), the connector status never changes and no
hotplug uevent is sent, so HDMI only appeared after a manual
echo detect > .../status.

Disable and re-enable polling just before drm_dev_register(), when the
connectors exist, so enable_hpd runs for each of them.

Checked on the tablet booted through the Microsoft UEFI: before the change
a debug trace showed no enable_hpd pass and hpd_cb=0x0 on every HPD
interrupt; after it the HDMI status follows the cable without any manual
detect.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/drm.c
@@ -559,6 +559,14 @@
 	err = aperture_remove_all_conflicting_devices(tegra_drm_driver.name);
 	if (err < 0)
 		goto hub;
+
+	/*
+	 * Output polling was initialised before the connectors existed, so its
+	 * enable_hpd pass found none and hotplug bridges (HDMI through
+	 * display-connector) never got their HPD callback. Run it again now.
+	 */
+	drm_kms_helper_poll_disable(drm);
+	drm_kms_helper_poll_enable(drm);
 
 	err = drm_dev_register(drm, 0);
 	if (err < 0)
